From: mscharged-port
Subject: Rollback: one-shot sounds only a replay played play late
Upstream-base: a353c8f2dfb34eb08fecd725965a46ea629428e3

The sounds started without a context (PlaySound, PlayOwnedSound with
none) end by themselves and nothing finds them again, so patches 0061
and 0062 leave them out: a replayed step played none, and one only the
replay had was lost. With predicted inputs that is the other player's
every new press, whose first step the replay alone runs as it is: a
deke, the mushroom's start and end, the first puff of Wario's gas, and
whatever the press does at once. Online, on the screen of the player
who did not press, such sounds came one time and not the next.

Outside replays each one played is now noted with its step, in the
audio's memory, which no rollback takes back (the last 512). A replay's
one looks for the same sound (slot and cue) played within 3 steps of its
own, as the presentation's sounds of a replayed step may fall in a frame
next to the first run's; each one played answers one replay's sound
once (the port's rollback counts the replays,
mscharged_rollback_audio_replay_start). One no step played waits for the
end of the rollback, with the tracked sounds' reconciliation, which plays
it then unless its step is more than 8 steps (160 ms) back. A sound only
the replaced timeline played has played; nothing takes it back.

